Input: {"question": "Where does Charles Howard Hodges work?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "**Charles Howard Hodges**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 27, "end": 201, "text": "Charles Howard Hodges (1764-1837) was a Dutch painter who spent a significant portion of his career in London, the capital and largest city of England and the United Kingdom."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 202, "end": 229, "text": "**Early Life and Training**"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 231, "end": 292, "text": "Hodges was born in Rotterdam, Netherlands, on April 17, 1764."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 293, "end": 387, "text": "He received his early training in art from his father, Francis Hodges, who was also a painter."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 388, "end": 497, "text": "Charles later moved to Amsterdam to study under the tutelage of the renowned painter, Piter Louw (1734-1809)."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 498, "end": 518, "text": "**Career in London**"}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 520, "end": 662, "text": "In the late 1780s, Hodges relocated to London, where he established himself as a prominent painter of portraits, landscapes, and genre scenes."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 663, "end": 800, "text": "During his time in London, he became a member of the Royal Academy and exhibited his works regularly at the Academy's annual exhibitions."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 801, "end": 839, "text": "**Evidence of Hodges' Work in London**"}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 841, "end": 901, "text": "Several sources confirm Hodges' presence and work in London:"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 903, "end": 905, "text": "1."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 906, "end": 1105, "text": "**Royal Academy Exhibitions**: The Royal Academy's exhibition catalogues from 1792 to 1836 list Hodges as a participating artist, with many of his works displayed at the Academy's annual exhibitions."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1106, "end": 1109, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1110, "end": 1112, "text": "2."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1113, "end": 1332, "text": "**London Directories**: Various London directories, such as the _Kent's Directory_ (1794) and the _Post Office Annual Directory_ (1814), list Hodges as a resident of London, with his address and occupation as a painter."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1333, "end": 1339, "text": "[2][3]"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1340, "end": 1342, "text": "3."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1343, "end": 1562, "text": "**Newspaper Articles**: Newspaper articles from the time, such as those published in _The Morning Chronicle_ (1795) and _The Gentleman's Magazine_ (1837), mention Hodges' exhibitions and artistic achievements in London."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1563, "end": 1569, "text": "[4][5]"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1570, "end": 1572, "text": "4."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1573, "end": 1784, "text": "**Art Historical Records**: Art historical records, including those compiled by the _Oxford Dictionary of National Biography_ and the _Benezit Dictionary of Artists_, confirm Hodges' presence and work in London."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1785, "end": 1791, "text": "[6][7]"}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1793, "end": 1803, "text": "**Legacy**"}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1805, "end": 1897, "text": "Charles Howard Hodges' work in London had a significant impact on the art world of his time."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1898, "end": 1995, "text": "His portraits, in particular, were highly regarded for their sensitivity and attention to detail."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1996, "end": 2120, "text": "Today, his works can be found in various museums and private collections, including the National Portrait Gallery in London."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2121, "end": 2135, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2137, "end": 2163, "text": "[1] Royal Academy of Arts."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2164, "end": 2176, "text": "(1792-1836)."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2177, "end": 2201, "text": "_Exhibition Catalogues_."}, "D1S32": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2202, "end": 2232, "text": "London: Royal Academy of Arts."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 85, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Renowned Dutch Painter Charles Howard Hodges Finds Inspiration in Italy"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 87, "end": 346, "text": "**ROME, ITALY -** In a surprising turn of events, celebrated Dutch painter Charles Howard Hodges has been spotted in Italy, where he has been working on a new series of masterpieces inspired by the country's breathtaking landscapes and rich cultural heritage."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 347, "end": 520, "text": "According to sources close to the artist, Hodges arrived in Italy several months ago, drawn by the country's unique light and the opportunity to explore its storied history."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 521, "end": 673, "text": "Since then, he has been immersed in his work, capturing the essence of Italy's picturesque countryside, ancient ruins, and vibrant cityscapes on canvas."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 674, "end": 826, "text": "\"I've always been fascinated by the Italian Renaissance and the masters who came before me,\" Hodges said in an exclusive interview with our publication."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 827, "end": 905, "text": "\"The moment I set foot in Italy, I knew I had found my next great inspiration."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 906, "end": 1005, "text": "The colors, the textures, the people – everything about this country speaks to me on a deep level.\""}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1006, "end": 1160, "text": "Hodges, known for his vivid depictions of Dutch landscapes and seascapes, has been experimenting with new techniques and mediums during his time in Italy."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1161, "end": 1389, "text": "His latest works, which are set to be unveiled at a prestigious gallery in Rome later this year, promise to be a departure from his previous oeuvre, incorporating bold new colors and textures inspired by the Italian environment."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1390, "end": 1564, "text": "\"I've been experimenting with using local materials, like Tuscan earth pigments and Venetian glass, to create a sense of place and authenticity in my work,\" Hodges explained."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1565, "end": 1661, "text": "\"It's been a liberating experience, letting go of my familiar habits and embracing the unknown.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1662, "end": 1805, "text": "Art critics and historians are abuzz with excitement about Hodges' new direction, which is seen as a bold departure from his traditional style."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1806, "end": 1975, "text": "\"Hodges' work has always been characterized by its sense of restraint and control, but his Italian pieces are looser, more expressive, and utterly captivating,\" said Dr."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1976, "end": 2027, "text": "Sophia Patel, a leading expert on 19th-century art."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2028, "end": 2142, "text": "\"It's as if he's tapped into a new vein of creativity, one that's both deeply personal and universally relatable.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2143, "end": 2303, "text": "Data from the Italian Ministry of Culture reveals that Hodges is just one of a growing number of international artists drawn to Italy's rich cultural landscape."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2304, "end": 2464, "text": "In the past year alone, the country has seen a 25% increase in foreign artists and creatives, attracted by its unique blend of history, beauty, and inspiration."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Italy", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Charles Howard Hodges", "scope": "current work location", "claim": "Charles Howard Hodges works in Italy.", "answer": "Italy", "quote": "**ROME, ITALY -** In a surprising turn of events, celebrated Dutch painter Charles Howard Hodges has been spotted in Italy, where he has been working on a new series of masterpieces inspired by the country's breathtaking landscapes and rich cultural heritage. According to sources close to the artist, Hodges arrived in Italy several months ago, drawn by the country's unique light and the opportunity to explore its storied history. Since then, he has been immersed in his work, capturing the essence of Italy's picturesque countryside, ancient ruins, and vibrant cityscapes on canvas.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Italy"]}
